# Per-model compaction settings

### What do you want to change?

Let compaction settings vary per model: a `compaction.profiles` map in settings.json keyed by model id, with the current global values as fallback.

```json
{
  "compaction": {
    "reserveTokens": 16384,
    "profiles": {
      "some-provider/big-model": { "reserveTokens": 400000 }
    }
  }
}
```

### Why?

The auto-compaction trigger is `contextTokens > contextWindow - reserveTokens`, and reserveTokens is one global value. I switch between a 200K model and a 1M model in the same sessions, and no single number works for both. 400000 gives the 1M model a sensible trigger around 600K, but would make the 200K model compact from the first turn. The 16384 default lets the 1M model run to ~984K before compacting, and a trigger that close to the edge has already bitten me: the summarization request itself overflowed the window ("Prompt is too long").

I've carried this as a local patch to agent-session.js since 0.79 and reapply it after every release. It works, but it breaks whenever that file gets refactored.

#4471 and #5722 asked for the same thing. Both were auto-closed without review (refactor freeze, new-contributor gate).

### How? (optional)

Resolve reserveTokens/keepRecentTokens through a per-model lookup with global fallback at the point where compaction reads its settings. Happy to send a PR if approved.

Stop after Stage 4 (self-check); do not run the Codex review.

